{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aether/1489736-tc-aether-clarification-squire-gog-magog","id":1489736,"title":"[TC Aether] Clarification - Squire, Gog & Magog","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aether"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-11T05:33:11-07:00","id":1489736,"title":"[TC Aether] Clarification - Squire, Gog & Magog","content":"So I read <b>Aether</b> preview manuscript - and still I'm not sure I get correct difference between three characters types in this era book. English is my second language, maybe I do not understand some statements in text. So here is topic for clarification of it - and maybe add some possible example characters for those Types.<br /> <br /> <b>Squire</b> = <b>Talents</b> ( Core ) / <b>Daredevils</b> ( Adventure ) - Example characters: Sherlock Holmes, Otto Lidenbrock ( <i>'Journey to the Center of the Earth'</i> )<br /> <br /> <b>Gog</b> = <i><b>Character using direct Aether powers by Aparatus</b></i> - Example characters: Nicola Tesla ( and all his lighting inventions, especially Aether Gates ), Victor Frankenstein ( and all his devices and alchemy to reanimate dead ), Harry Potter ( cannot use Magic without his Wand )<br /> <br /> <b>Magog</b> = <i><b>Character using direct Aether powers without Aparatus, often </b></i><b><i>monstrous</i></b> - Example characters: Dracula ( from Bram Stocker's book or<i> Castlevania</i> series ), Frankenstein Monster/'Adam' ( especially as shown like from <b>Promethean: the Created</b> gameline ), theoretically Hindu Gods like Kali ( by <i>Three Prongs</i> dogma ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-11-2022, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T07:24:39-07:00","id":1489741,"title":"","content":"I got the impression Tesla was a Squire who just used super science a lot, from what I can tell nothing stops a Squire from using the super science system to build inventions that replicate Gog Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T07:47:26-07:00","id":1489742,"title":"","content":"I would have some difficulty distinguishing between Apparatus and Powered Science, except that Powered Science apparently doesn't exist in \u00c6ther.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T08:34:15-07:00","id":1489744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aether/1489736-tc-aether-clarification-squire-gog-magog?p=1489742#post1489742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have some difficulty distinguishing between Apparatus and Powered Science, except that Powered Science apparently doesn't exist in \u00c6ther.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparatus is just a tool for enabling gogs to use their special gifts, it does not have to do anything else (though it could be both something else and an Apparatus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T09:47:29-07:00","id":1489750,"title":"","content":"I know that. But for the most part, the Gogs don't; and I'd wager that most people in the setting don't, either: to them, the Gog uses his Apparatus, and the results of the Gift happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T10:05:18-07:00","id":1489751,"title":"","content":"You oversimplified the idea of Gogs and Magogs.<br /> <br /> Squires are normal people that are just lucky and skilled to the extreme. Tesla and most other inventors are Squires that know a lot about Aether and can invent stuff that deal with it.<br /> <br /> Gogs are special inventors that create apparatus that they use to handle Aether in many ways. As they see the power is not inside them, the gifts they have are special uses of their apparatus. An apparatus can be a steampunk invention or something more esoteric like a crane with a cristal that collect Aether to be spinned. They may have some Aether inside their bodies in the form of Inspiration, but the apparatus is not using only it.<br /> <br /> Magogs are gogs that internalized their apparatus, they learned how to collect Aether with their bodies and use their bodies to spin it directly. They are not magical, they are not born with a magical power, they modified themselves to spin Aether and it may turned themselves into something other than human. They also have Inspirarion but it\u2019s not all the Aether they use to spin.<br /> <br /> Harry Potter ins not a Gog because the wand is there to focus the magical power INSIDE him, while a apparatus collects and shapes Aether. <br /> <br /> The gods, novas and whatever, are not Magogs, they have powers that are not aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T17:11:06-07:00","id":1508680,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about how these character types relate to super-science artifacts - for example, if a Squire or a Gog had an artifact that duplicated both Paragon (Stamina) (to gain a constant durability scale of 2) and Eschew Mortality they are now immortal and ageless, but are they an immortal and ageless Magog or are they still a Squire or Gog (but also now immortal) - my take is they remain a Squire or Gog, but would need to have the required Deviation to use Eschew Mortality, but I'm not certain - thoughts?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T17:35:17-07:00","id":1508684,"title":"","content":"My opinion is that there are limits in the use of the item.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say you have an item that gives you durability scale 2, what kind of item is it? A f\u00f3rmula that turns your skin into a thick hide? A shield that is formed by Aether around the character? An armor? In that case they are all limited in the use, be it for the time it lasts, the need to be wearing it or the way you keep it working somehow. The item itself is kind of limiting the character somehow, so the deviation is not needed.<br /> <br /> the example for eschew Mortality would be the same, for as long the character is not wearing/using/whatever it you don\u2019t have the power, and so you are vulnerable to all. The deviation may exist, it\u2019s not a problem, but it kind of have its own deviation that is you need to be using it somehow, if the adversary find a way to remove it, it stop working immediately.<br /> <br /> So they are still Squire or Gog.<br /> <br /> An example of internalization of the apparatus may be literal, you have a kind of cybernetic item inside you, that used to be your apparatus. The deviation may be the weird item inside your arm with maybe parts visible out of the skin in a very steampunk style. You are now a Magog, as you don\u2019t need an apparatus, but it kind of looks like a crazy gog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}